es the  Aquaman trailer was as The Hollywood  Reporter put it the best received at  comic-con our appetite has definitely  been wet there was worse pep talk ever  worse the James Gunn double whammy  even though Marvel Studios skipped  comic-con they still managed to make the  biggest headlines but not in a good way  on Friday July 20th the second day of  comic-con  it was announced that writer and  director  James Gunn had been fired from guardians  of the galaxy vol 3 after a conservative  website enough some controversial tweets  Gunn posted prior to landing his gig  with Marvel gonna been scheduled to  appear at Sony's Comicon panel later  that evening to announce a secret  project but in the wake of his firing  that appearance was cancelled as well  leaving the status of the project up in  the air  Gunn getting fired and then not  appearing at SDCC was a two-fold shocker  one Twitter user best summed up it's  crazy that the only thing the MCU  brought to Comic Con this year was a  firing of James Gunn best the glass  trailer nearly two decades after his  2000 hit and breakable director M night  Shyamalan finally unveiled the trailer  for the long-awaited sequel glass which  also acts as a follow-up to 2017 split  stylish wonderfully self-aware sprinkled  with action and featuring Sarah Paulsen  as a psychiatrist who specializes in  treating super-powered people glass  looks to be an ambitious return to form  we can't wait to see how it all turns  out worse the Johnny Depp debacle after  unleashing a magical trailer for  fantastic beasts the crimes of  Grindelwald Warner Brothers gave  comic-con a rollicking good time with a  panel featuring stars Jude Law and Ezra  Miller unfortunately those good times  turned a little sour when embattled  actor Johnny Depp showed up in full  costume as the villainous Gellert  Grindelwald appearing to a very mixed  reaction of cheers &amp; boos depp press  forward with a pre-written monologue but  for some funds the appearance w